    "content": "Chuck Norris is best known for starring as Cordell Walker in the hit CBS television series Walker, Texas Ranger (1993–2001), a modern-day lawman upholding the code of the Old West. Previously, he starred as the rugged Ranger J.J. McQuade in the 1983 film Lone Wolf McQuade, which served as the inspiration for the TV series. Key Aspects of Chuck Norris as a Texas Ranger: Walker, Texas Ranger (TV Series): Norris played Sgt. Cordell Walker, a Vietnam vet, martial arts expert, and half-Cherokee lawman based in Dallas. The show was a ratings success for eight seasons, featuring Clarence Gilyard Jr. as his partner James Trivette. Lone Wolf McQuade (1983 Film): Norris starred as J.J. McQuade, a gritty, \"lone wolf\" Ranger who battles arms dealers, setting the archetype for his later TV role. Action Style: Both roles defined by a mix of martial arts, intense combat, and a strong, unwavering moral code, which became iconic in 1990s action television. Multiple Roles: In the series, Norris also played 19th-century lawman Hayes Cooper, a historical figure admired by Walker. This video features an action-packed scene from the film 'Lone Wolf McQuade':38sAmazon MGM StudiosYouTube• Aug 12, 2024 38s",
